{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction_gt_one_of_pi_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction_gt_one_of_pi_bound","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L207-L216","doc":"The Habiro (archimedean `ρ_∞`) action `π²/5 ≈ 1.974` is not the geometric\n(root-of-unity / state-integral) action `Vol(4₁)/π ≈ 0.646`: they differ by\nmore than `1` — the `ħ ↔ 2πi/N` wall.  Stated via an explicit numeric\nseparation (`Vol(4₁)/π < 1 < π²/5`); the two constants sit in different\nnumber fields (`ℚ(√−3)` vs `ℚ(√5)`), computed in\n`qbeta_fourone_habiro_tail_action_probe.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction_eq_pi_sq_div_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction_eq_pi_sq_div_five","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L195-L205","doc":"**The 4₁ Habiro-tail resurgent action equals `π²/5`.**\n\nDerived: substitute the integral representation and the *derived* golden\nvalue `li2_inv_phi_sq`; the `ln²φ` cancels, leaving `π²/5`.  This is the\narchimedean `ρ_∞` action — **distinct** from the geometric (root-of-unity /\nstate-integral) action `Vol(4₁)/π ≈ 0.646` (the `ħ ↔ 2πi/N` wall, exact). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:habiro-tail-archimedean-action","label":"prop:habiro-tail-archimedean-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/habiro-tail-archimedean-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroAction","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L191-L193","doc":"The 4₁ Habiro-tail resurgent action `A₀ = -4 ∫₀^{ln φ} ln(2 sinh s) ds`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.integral_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.integral_eq","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L187-L187","doc":"Its closed form in terms of the golden dilogarithm value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.integralLogSinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.integralLogSinh","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L185-L185","doc":"`∫₀^{ln φ} ln(2 sinh s) ds`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.mk","kind":"ctor","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L183-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.toClassicalDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral.toClassicalDilog","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L183-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.LogSinhIntegral","kind":"class","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L179-L189","doc":"Cited input: the `log(2 sinh)` integral representation\n`∫₀^{ln φ} ln(2 sinh s) ds = (ln φ)²/2 + (Li₂(φ⁻²) − π²/6)/2`\n(from `ln(2 sinh s) = s + ln(1 − e^{−2s})` and\n`∫₀^x ln(1 − e^{−2s}) ds = (Li₂(e^{−2x}) − π²/6)/2`, `e^{−2 ln φ} = φ⁻²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.li2_inv_phi_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.li2_inv_phi_sq","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L139-L175","doc":"**Classically intricate value — DERIVED, not axiomatized.**\n\n`Li₂(φ⁻²) = π²/15 − ln²φ`, obtained from the three functional equations\nat `x = ψ = φ⁻¹` by linear elimination, using\n`1 − ψ = ψ²`, `1 + ψ = φ`, `ψ/(1+ψ) = ψ²`, `log ψ = − log φ`, and\n`log(ψ²) = 2 log ψ`.\n\nDerivation (with `a = Li₂ ψ`, `b = Li₂ ψ²`, `c = Li₂(−ψ)`):\n* reflection: `a + b = π²/6 − 2 ln²φ`\n* duplication: `a + c = b/2`\n* landen: `c = −b − ½ ln²φ`\n⇒ `a = (3/2) b + ½ ln²φ` ⇒ `(5/2) b = π²/6 − (5/2) ln²φ`\n⇒ `b = π²/15 − ln²φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.landen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.landen","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L137-L137","doc":"**Landen**: `Li₂(-x) = − Li₂(x/(1+x)) − ½ ln²(1+x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.duplication","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.duplication","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L135-L135","doc":"**Duplication**: `Li₂(x) + Li₂(-x) = ½ Li₂(x²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.reflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.reflection","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L133-L133","doc":"**Euler reflection**: `Li₂(x) + Li₂(1-x) = π²/6 − ln x · ln(1-x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.Li2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.Li2","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L131-L131","doc":"The real dilogarithm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.ClassicalDilog","kind":"class","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L124-L137","doc":"The three standard real-dilogarithm functional equations, packaged as a\nconditional class (each field is a *cited* identity — Lewin, and analytically\nproved in [hakimoglu-brown2025]).  `Li2` is the real dilogarithm on `(-∞, 1]`;\nthe fields are used only at the golden points, where every argument lies in\nrange. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroFactor_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroFactor_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L113-L120","doc":"**The 4₁ Habiro tail factor is bar-even** (`q ↔ q⁻¹`-invariant, `q ≠ 0`),\nso `S(q) = S(q⁻¹)`: no bar-odd datum (4₁ amphichirality; #3923 null).\n⇒ the odd-channel b3ix needs the chiral 5₂ tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.habiroFactor","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L108-L111","doc":"The `j`-th factor of the 4₁ Habiro cyclotomic tail at real `q`:\n`(1 - q^j)(1 - q^{-j})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.log_inv_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.log_inv_phi","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L102-L104","doc":"`log ψ = - log φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.inv_div_one_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.inv_div_one_add","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L97-L100","doc":"`ψ/(1+ψ) = ψ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.one_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.one_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L90-L95","doc":"`1 + ψ = φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.one_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.one_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L86-L88","doc":"`1 - ψ = ψ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.inv_add_inv_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.inv_add_inv_sq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L79-L84","doc":"`ψ + ψ² = 1` where `ψ = φ⁻¹` (from `φ² = φ + 1` divided by `φ²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_sq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L72-L77","doc":"`φ² = φ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_ne","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi_pos","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L67-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.sqrt5_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.sqrt5_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailAction.phi","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailAction.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The golden ratio `φ = (1 + √5)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}